219
00:08:36.532 --> 00:08:38.267
Some confusion.

220
00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:42.032
I'm proud to announce that my instinct was correct, Adam.

221
00:08:42.032 --> 00:08:42.974
It was.

222
00:08:42.974 --> 00:08:45.899
Per Merriam Webster, bi-weekly is defined as

223
00:08:45.899 --> 00:08:50.441
something that occurs every two weeks or twice per week.

224
00:08:50.441 --> 00:08:51.274
That's confusing.

225
00:08:51.274 --> 00:08:53.977
How is that possible?

226
00:08:53.977 --> 00:08:55.674
Because even Mariam doesn't know what it means.

227
00:08:55.674 --> 00:08:56.507
Right.

228
00:08:56.507 --> 00:08:57.984
It means both or either?

229
00:08:57.984 --> 00:08:58.817
Yes.

230
00:08:58.817 --> 00:09:00.419
This is sewing mass confusion.

231
00:09:00.419 --> 00:09:01.472
I blame gen Z.

232
00:09:01.472 --> 00:09:02.324
Similarly...

233
00:09:02.324 --> 00:09:03.865
No, it's always been the case.

234
00:09:03.865 --> 00:09:06.788
Similarly, bi-monthly is defined as

235
00:09:06.788 --> 00:09:10.621
something that occurs every other month, or...

236
00:09:12.646 --> 00:09:15.083
No, every other month or twice a month.

237
00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:16.140
This is not good.

238
00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.169
So if you say we're gonna meet bi-monthly,

239
00:09:18.169 --> 00:09:19.590
or we're gonna meet bi-weekly...

240
00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:20.423
Right.

241
00:09:20.423 --> 00:09:22.841
How are you supposed to know what that means?

242
00:09:22.841 --> 00:09:25.887
If you like join a new organization,

243
00:09:25.887 --> 00:09:28.891
and then the organization says, "Okay, great to be here.

244
00:09:28.891 --> 00:09:31.500
We're gonna be here by bi-weekly."

245
00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.688
And then you don't come for two weeks,

246
00:09:33.688 --> 00:09:35.157
and you've missed three meetings.

247
00:09:35.157 --> 00:09:36.618
(laughter)

248
00:09:36.618 --> 00:09:37.963
Or at least two meetings.

249
00:09:37.963 --> 00:09:38.917
That's not good.

250
00:09:38.917 --> 00:09:39.750
No.

251
00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:40.583
You're on the outs, buddy.

252
00:09:40.583 --> 00:09:42.916
So, with this, hence forth

253
00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:46.922
I despair over the pitfalls of the English language.

254
00:09:46.922 --> 00:09:49.969
I mean, come on, words term, they have one job.

255
00:09:49.969 --> 00:09:50.869
One job.

256
00:09:50.869 --> 00:09:53.383
And this means two different things,

257
00:09:53.383 --> 00:09:54.398
I don't know what to tell you.

258
00:09:54.398 --> 00:09:56.425
Let's create a new word for it.

259
00:09:56.425 --> 00:09:57.561
What's that?

260
00:09:57.561 --> 00:09:59.478
For every other week.

261
00:10:01.328 --> 00:10:02.161
You blanked out.

262
00:10:02.161 --> 00:10:04.205
Too much pressure.
Yeah, I know.

263
00:10:04.205 --> 00:10:05.276
