when that goes away,

1305
00:55:44.861 --> 00:55:48.578
you see the core true nature of their goals.

1306
00:55:48.578 --> 00:55:51.934
And most of them have been raised in these Madrasas,

1307
00:55:51.934 --> 00:55:55.886
they've never been exposed to any kind of education.

1308
00:55:55.886 --> 00:55:56.972
They've never had internet,

1309
00:55:56.972 --> 00:55:58.470
they don't know what the world looks like,

1310
00:55:58.470 --> 00:56:00.434
or what exists in the world.

1311
00:56:00.434 --> 00:56:04.652
They have no concept of democracy and justice.

1312
00:56:04.652 --> 00:56:09.390
And their whole aim is to essentially shroud women,

1313
00:56:09.390 --> 00:56:11.708
and implement sharia law, that's it.

1314
00:56:11.708 --> 00:56:13.721
And these are the leaders and that's the scariest thing.

1315
00:56:13.721 --> 00:56:17.902
And I was looking at an interview, where this man,

1316
00:56:17.902 --> 00:56:21.934
he's I think the second person in the leadership right now.

1317
00:56:21.934 --> 00:56:23.530
He's probably in his twenties.

1318
00:56:23.530 --> 00:56:25.273
And he was talking about women's rights.

1319
00:56:25.273 --> 00:56:28.440
Said, "Well, we believe that women should have rights.

1320
00:56:28.440 --> 00:56:29.970
Women are our mothers,

1321
00:56:29.970 --> 00:56:33.410
they're the representation of the society."

1322
00:56:33.410 --> 00:56:36.822
And then suddenly you could see that these statements,

1323
00:56:36.822 --> 00:56:38.265
I think he kind of ran out of words

1324
00:56:38.265 --> 00:56:40.715
that were told to him to say.

1325
00:56:40.715 --> 00:56:42.380
And it just flipped into something like,

1326
00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:46.917
"Well, they have to be covered, because that's the rule,

1327
00:56:46.917 --> 00:56:48.000
that's the law."

1328
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:51.623
And I was telling Dean, they brought up an example.

1329
00:56:51.623 --> 00:56:53.202
So this is the analogy that he used.

1330
00:56:53.202 --> 00:56:55.700
He said, "Well, if you go to a farmer's market,

1331
00:56:55.700 --> 00:56:57.405
and you see melons, right?

1332
00:56:57.405 --> 00:56:59.119
There is a split melon,

1333
00:56:59.119 --> 00:57:02.103
and then there's a whole covered melon.

1334
00:57:02.103 --> 00:57:03.925
Would you buy the covered melon,

1335
00:57:03.925 --> 00:57:05.708
or would you buy the split melon?

1336
00:57:05.708 --> 00:57:07.967
The split melon has a lot of germs on it,

1337
00:57:07.967 --> 00:57:10.009
and there's a lot of bugs on it.

1338
00:57:10.009 --> 00:57:11.171
That's not sweet.

1339
00:57:11.171 --> 00:57:12.922
That's not sweet enough for the husband.

1340
00:57:12.922 --> 00:57:13.915
The shrouded melon

1341
00:57:13.915 --> 00:57:16.093
is the one that you would go and buy one."

1342
00:57:16.093 --> 00:57:18.909
So he basically gave an example of how women should be,

1343
00:57:18.909 --> 00:57:21.024
by just giving an example of melon.

1344
00:57:21.024 --> 00:57:24.478
This is the second highest person in the leadership.

1345
00:57:24.478 --> 00:57:27.103
The scariest conversation I've ever heard in my life.

1346
00:57:27.103 --> 00:57:29.612
That's how they think.

1347
00:57:29.612 --> 00:57:33.195
Despite that, we have this US occupation.

1348
00:57:34.886 --> 00:57:39.553
And with that a creep of urban progressive ways of life,

1349
00:57:41.266 --> 00:57:45.599
that starts to infiltrate the culture on some level.

1350
00:57:46.624 --> 00:57:50.864
But Afghanistan historically being this nation of survivors,

1351
00:57:50.864 --> 00:57:53.767
that have defied empires for millennia,

1352
00:57:53.767 --> 00:57:57.850
my sense is that most people are going to behave,

1353
00:58:00.345 --> 00:58:05.130
in a manner that is survivor expedient for them.

1354
00:58:05.130 --> 00:58:07.705
And when you have US troops there,

1355
00:58:07.705 --> 00:58:08.538
who can say,

1356
00:58:08.538 --> 00:58:11.231
"Well, I don't know how long I'm gonna be here,

1357
00:58:11.231 --> 00:58:13.277
but you have to pledge allegiance to us."

1358
00:58:13.277 --> 00:58:16.228
And knowing that next week the Taliban is gonna come,

1359
00:58:16.228 --> 00:58:18.346
and place the same demands on these people,

1360
00:58:18.346 --> 00:58:21.090
people are gonna do what they need to do to survive.

1361
00:58:21.090 --> 00:58:25.337
And so it's hard to get a gauge on the temperature...

1362
00:58:25.337 --> 00:58:26.578
If you do a temperature check,

1363
00:58:26.578 --> 00:58:31.286
on where people's values are, and what they aspire to do,

1364
00:58:31.286 --> 00:58:34.900
what they aspire to in their own lives it seems murky

1365
00:58:34.900 --> 00:58:39.217
in terms of trying to really understand the culture.

1366
00:58:39.217 --> 00:58:40.702
'Cause there is no monoculture.

1367
00:58:40.702 --> 00:58:41.785
No, no, no.

1368
00:58:42.794 --> 00:58:46.433
It's such an accurate statement in the sense that,

1369
00:58:46.433 --> 00:58:48.052
the expression...

1370
00:58:48.052 --> 00:58:53.052
Even the people in themselves are in such turmoil right now,

1371
00:58:53.689 --> 00:58:58.689
that not only is their language mercurial and capricious

1372
00:58:59.153 --> 00:59:03.700
and floating and amoebic, but even their values are that.

1373
00:59:03.700 --> 00:59:05.903
And it's not a judgment of them.

1374
00:59:05.903 --> 00:59:07.264
It is-

1375
00:59:07.264 --> 00:59:08.479
Survival.
It's survival.

1376
00:59:08.479 --> 00:59:10.315
I mean, none of us have experienced that.

1377
00:59:10.315 --> 00:59:11.687
I mean, what's the worst thing

1378
00:59:11.687 --> 00:59:13.356
I experienced in Redondo Beach?

1379
00:59:13.356 --> 00:59:15.606
(laughter)

1380
00:59:18.006 --> 00:59:20.956
Yeah, sometimes these young people drive really fast across,

1381
00:59:20.956 --> 00:59:21.946
in front of my house.

1382
00:59:21.946 --> 00:59:22.779
(laughs)

1383
00:59:22.779 --> 00:59:24.578
Probably that's the biggest one.

1384
00:59:24.578 --> 00:59:26.365
But to know...

1385
00:59:26.365 --> 00:59:28.049
When I went there these families said that,

1386
00:59:28.049 --> 00:59:29.813
"Right before you guys came during Taliban,

1387
00:59:29.813 --> 00:59:31.353
there were rockets being fired every day,

1388
00:59:31.353 --> 00:59:34.757
and every family member had a person that had been killed

1389
00:59:34.757 --> 00:59:35.983
during the war."

1390
00:59:35.983 --> 00:59:39.256
Every single family member killed.

1391
00:59:39.256 --> 00:59:41.327
We don't have any idea of that.

1392
00:59:41.327 --> 00:59:43.446
So you're right, it's survival now.

1393
00:59:43.446 --> 00:59:46.297
And it's at the pace of the vacuum,

1394
00:59:46.297 --> 00:59:48.454
and the vacuum is the thing, right?

1395
00:59:48.454 --> 00:59:50.954
The vacuum that's left behind.

1396
00:59:51.910 --> 00:59:53.976
So we've started this organization called

1397
00:59:53.976 --> 00:59:56.057
Restore Her Hope, and the-

1398
00:59:56.057 --> 00:59:57.140
Restore Her Voice.

1399
00:59:57.140 --> 00:59:57.973
Her Voice.

1400
00:59:57.973 --> 00:59:59.472
I keep coming back to hope.

1401
00:59:59.472 --> 01:00:00.757
Cause you're looking for hope.

1402
01:00:00.757 --> 01:00:01.590
I'm looking for hope,

1403
01:00:01.590 --> 01:00:03.430
Restore Her Voice, because we said, "Where can we help?

1404
01:00:03.430 --> 01:00:04.601
Where can we help?"

1405
01:00:04.601 --> 01:00:05.434
Not just in Afghanistan,

1406
01:00:05.434 --> 01:00:08.849
because we're women's rights and justice and all that.

1407
01:00:08.849 --> 01:00:10.312
And it's gonna be broader.

1408
01:00:10.312 --> 01:00:13.358
It's not going to be us going there and saving people.

1409
01:00:13.358 --> 01:00:16.719
My goodness, I couldn't even do some pushups, as you heard.

1410
01:00:16.719 --> 01:00:20.157
I'm not a warrior, I'm a scientist.

1411
01:00:20.157 --> 01:00:21.447
What's the most effective...

1412
01:00:21.447 --> 01:00:22.783
And this is important.

1413
01:00:22.783 --> 01:00:26.402
What's the most effective unit of a society.

1414
01:00:26.402 --> 01:00:28.927
And we have three men here and...

1415
01:00:28.927 --> 01:00:32.039
Well, four, and one woman here,

1416
01:00:32.039 --> 01:00:34.416
the most effective unit of productivity

1417
01:00:34.416 --> 01:00:36.252
in a society are the women,

1418
01:00:36.252 --> 01:00:39.475
a dollar spent in healthcare and on women,

1419
01:00:39.475 --> 01:00:41.672
is at the minimum four times more effective

1420
01:00:41.672 --> 01:00:43.255
than anything else.

1421
01:00:44.113 --> 01:00:47.215
And the same is true across all spectrums.

1422
01:00:47.215 --> 01:00:49.944
And when you give women voice,

1423
01:00:49.944 --> 01:00:52.812
especially if they've been empowered already,

1424
01:00:52.812 --> 01:00:56.127
that becomes the most powerful force in the society,

1425
01:00:56.127 --> 01:00:57.377
positive force.

1426
01:00:58.468 --> 01:01:00.337
And in United States or other places,

1427
01:01:00.337 --> 01:01:01.954
when you take women's rights away,

1428
01:01:01.954 --> 01:01:03.566
when you take their voices away,

1429
01:01:03.566 --> 01:01:08.566
it becomes the nightest of the most destructive cycle.

1430
01:01:08.574 --> 01:01:11.943
In fact, I think that's the beginning of a fall.

1431
01:01:11.943 --> 01:01:13.770
So that's why we thought that,

1432
01:01:13.770 --> 01:01:15.966
giving women their voices back,

1433
01:01:15.966 --> 01:01:19.710
both Afghan or otherwise especially post-traumatic,

1434
01:01:19.710 --> 01:01:22.445
is I think the most effective thing we could do.

1435
01:01:22.445 --> 01:01:23.278
So what do you do?

1436
01:01:23.278 --> 01:01:27.028
What's the organization do like specifically?

1437
01:01:28.396 --> 01:01:32.146
Our goal is to highlight and promote women,

1438
01:01:33.723 --> 01:01:35.646
who have lived in Afghanistan,

1439
01:01:35.646 --> 01:01:40.281
who have been through the trauma for them to be the voice,

1440
01:01:40.281 --> 01:01:41.736
and for them to be the platform

1441
01:01:41.736 --> 01:01:43.979
for all women living in Afghanistan,

1442
01:01:43.979 --> 01:01:45.354
and in any other country.

1443
01:01:45.354 --> 01:01:47.506
I think the stories that they tell,

1444
01:01:47.506 --> 01:01:50.949
the kind of perspective that they give us is invaluable,

1445
01:01:50.949 --> 01:01:53.852
because it really touches the true core

1446
01:01:53.852 --> 01:01:57.585
of who we are as a society, and as human beings.

1447
01:01:57.585 --> 01:02:00.033
And we want to provide them

1448
01:02:00.033 --> 01:02:03.056
not necessarily just the same platform they had,

1449
01:02:03.056 --> 01:02:04.750
all these brave and courageous women

1450
01:02:04.750 --> 01:02:06.175
who've fled the country,

1451
01:02:06.175 --> 01:02:07.863
the same platform here in the United States,

1452
01:02:07.863 --> 01:02:10.976
but to help them get to the right people,

1453
01:02:10.976 --> 01:02:12.988
the right groups, the right organizations,

1454
01:02:12.988 --> 01:02:15.214
to be able to promote this message,

1455
01:02:15.214 --> 01:02:17.595
that women's rights is human rights.

1456
01:02:17.595 --> 01:02:20.936
And they need to be at the same seat,

1457
01:02:20.936 --> 01:02:24.734
if not at a higher seat of making decisions for themselves,

1458
01:02:24.734 --> 01:02:26.026
and for this world.

1459
01:02:26.026 --> 01:02:28.361
We have incredible politicians,

1460
01:02:28.361 --> 01:02:31.408
YouTubers, artists, scientists,

1461
01:02:31.408 --> 01:02:34.241
who have been forced out of the country.

1462
01:02:34.241 --> 01:02:37.289
And so we're trying to welcome them.

1463
01:02:37.289 --> 01:02:39.615
We're trying to give them some stable ground,

1464
01:02:39.615 --> 01:02:43.110
and let them speak for the country.

1465
01:02:43.110 --> 01:02:45.759
So it's the platform for these various women

1466
01:02:45.759 --> 01:02:46.964
of different backgrounds?

1467
01:02:46.964 --> 01:02:48.589
Yeah, absolutely.

1468
01:02:48.589 --> 01:02:49.422
Right.

1469
01:02:49.422 --> 01:02:51.470
Like this diaspora of women.

1470
01:02:51.470 --> 01:02:54.517
Where are some of these women who have gotten out,

1471
01:02:54.517 --> 01:02:55.809
where are they settling,

1472
01:02:55.809 --> 01:02:57.589
or are they just spread out all over the place?

1473
01:02:57.589 --> 01:03:01.152
What is the kind of refugee landscape look like?

1474
01:03:01.152 --> 01:03:02.323
They've been spread out.

1475
01:03:02.323 --> 01:03:04.861
Yeah, it's a little chaotic right now.

1476
01:03:04.861 --> 01:03:06.023
The women we were talking about,

1477
01:03:06.023 --> 01:03:08.730
and we've identified a few of them are in Washington DC.

1478
01:03:08.730 --> 01:03:13.017
And some of them are actually in Los Angeles area as well.

1479
01:03:13.017 --> 01:03:14.685
What happened was a huge number of people

1480
01:03:14.685 --> 01:03:17.687
were brought out to Qatar and other places, Germany.

1481
01:03:17.687 --> 01:03:20.030
And then from there to US, and other places.

1482
01:03:20.030 --> 01:03:24.718
And in US, they're kept in big spaces in Washington

1483
01:03:24.718 --> 01:03:26.887
and Dallas and other places.

1484
01:03:26.887 --> 01:03:29.700
But the women that we are talking about,

1485
01:03:29.700 --> 01:03:31.300
they were leaders of their fields.

1486
01:03:31.300 --> 01:03:32.596
For example, there's a woman

1487
01:03:32.596 --> 01:03:36.225
that was the head of the Orchestra,

1488
01:03:36.225 --> 01:03:38.268
and actually played in Kennedy Center, right?

1489
01:03:38.268 --> 01:03:39.721
So she's in the United States.

1490
01:03:39.721 --> 01:03:40.883
We're hoping to give her the platform,

1491
01:03:40.883 --> 01:03:43.903
to not just get to where she was before,

1492
01:03:43.903 --> 01:03:45.611
but also speak about that.

1493
01:03:45.611 --> 01:03:47.769
I really think the most important thing as human beings

1494
01:03:47.769 --> 01:03:49.351
we can do, is speak.

1495
01:03:49.351 --> 01:03:53.574
Speak fearlessly, speak often, speak with errors,

1496
01:03:53.574 --> 01:03:55.991
make mistakes, but speak, speak, speak,

1497
01:03:55.991 --> 01:03:57.577
and speak the truth without any abatement,

1498
01:03:57.577 --> 01:04:00.831
nobody's telling us not say certain things.

1499
01:04:00.831 --> 01:04:05.545
And out of that, that's a pair of phenomenon of evolution,

1500
01:04:05.545 --> 01:04:08.839
that sped up revolution billion times,

1501
01:04:08.839 --> 01:04:10.840
our ability to speak fearlessly.

1502
01:04:10.840 --> 01:04:12.587
And if these women who have the power,

1503
01:04:12.587 --> 01:04:15.898
who have the tools, who've lived those experiences,

1504
01:04:15.898 --> 01:04:19.639
I think there will be a megaphone for the cause.

1505
01:04:19.639 --> 01:04:21.772
And it also highlights how similar we are.

1506
01:04:21.772 --> 01:04:22.605
And when we speak,

1507
01:04:22.605 --> 01:04:26.772
we realized that all those artificial differences,

1508
01:04:27.809 --> 01:04:29.734
whether it's language, or the way we dress,

1509
01:04:29.734 --> 01:04:33.798
or the way we speak, or we carry ourselves it just false.

1510
01:04:33.798 --> 01:04:36.823
One of the things that we are trying to do,

1511
01:04:36.823 --> 01:04:40.330
is to make every American living here in the United States

1512
01:04:40.330 --> 01:04:41.361
and around the world,

1513
01:04:41.361 --> 01:04:43.911
for them to feel that these women are them.

1514
01:04:43.911 --> 01:04:46.930
They are you, they're the neighbor that you have,

1515
01:04:46.930 --> 01:04:49.000
they're your mom, they're like your sister.

1516
01:04:49.000 --> 01:04:50.097
They're like your daughter.

1517
01:04:50.097 --> 01:04:51.382
They're like your friend.

1518
01:04:51.382 --> 01:04:52.673
They're no different.

1519
01:04:52.673 --> 01:04:56.165
And if we can shorten the distance

1520
01:04:56.165 --> 01:04:58.410
between those differences,

1521
01:04:58.410 --> 01:05:01.067
and engage in conversations with them.

1522
01:05:01.067 --> 01:05:04.251
I think we can all work towards a better world.

1523
01:05:04.251 --> 01:05:06.670
We can be better versions of ourselves.

1524
01:05:06.670 --> 01:05:09.398
Adam mentioned the short documentary

1525
01:05:09.398 --> 01:05:11.608
"Learning to Skateboard."

1526
01:05:11.608 --> 01:05:12.441
What's it called?

1527
01:05:12.441 --> 01:05:13.274
In a war torn.

1528
01:05:13.274 --> 01:05:14.744
In a War Zone.
In a War Zone.

1529
01:05:14.744 --> 01:05:17.285
If you're a girl.
If you're a girl.

1530
01:05:17.285 --> 01:05:20.220
Which I believe won the Oscar, in 2019.

1531
01:05:20.220 --> 01:05:21.239
(crosstalk drowns out the speaker)

1532
01:05:21.239 --> 01:05:23.270
I watched it this morning and I was literally weeping,

1533
01:05:23.270 --> 01:05:25.626
because to watch that movie now,

1534
01:05:25.626 --> 01:05:27.543
in the context of what's transpired

1535
01:05:27.543 --> 01:05:29.210
over the last couple of weeks.

1536
01:05:29.210 --> 01:05:32.197
It's so heart wrenching and you can't help but think,

1537
01:05:32.197 --> 01:05:34.465
"Where are these young women now?

1538
01:05:34.465 --> 01:05:35.579
And what are they doing?

1539
01:05:35.579 --> 01:05:38.448
And is there any possibility or hope,

1540
01:05:38.448 --> 01:05:42.425
for getting people out of the country at this point?"

1541
01:05:42.425 --> 01:05:45.817
We all bore witness to what transpired at the airport.

1542
01:05:45.817 --> 01:05:49.262
But with the Taliban stranglehold

1543
01:05:49.262 --> 01:05:51.321
on the country at the moment,

1544
01:05:51.321 --> 01:05:54.485
there doesn't seem to be an opportunity.

1545
01:05:54.485 --> 01:05:56.488
Unfortunately not.

1546
01:05:56.488 --> 01:06:01.367
We're seeing this diminishing of the efforts at this point.

1547
01:06:01.367 --> 01:06:03.736
And trying not to lose hope,

1548
01:06:03.736 --> 01:06:06.316
and it's difficult not to lose hope

1549
01:06:06.316 --> 01:06:08.348
at this point, to be honest.

1550
01:06:08.348 --> 01:06:11.511
To make it my field, our field, neurology.

1551
01:06:11.511 --> 01:06:14.618
So we're a big signal detecting device, right?

1552
01:06:14.618 --> 01:06:16.148
Our brain.

1553
01:06:16.148 --> 01:06:18.805
We don't get out of our comfort,

1554
01:06:18.805 --> 01:06:22.013
unless something happens, that gets out of comfort, right?

1555
01:06:22.013 --> 01:06:23.098
And for millions of years,

1556
01:06:23.098 --> 01:06:24.638
that was because we had the distinguish

1557
01:06:24.638 --> 01:06:27.134
between a bush and a lion.

1558
01:06:27.134 --> 01:06:29.175
Now it's a little more complex,

1559
01:06:29.175 --> 01:06:31.412
human behavior, social aspects.

