2259
01:35:28.584 --> 01:35:30.033
and eliminate that?

2260
01:35:30.033 --> 01:35:30.866
That's a good question.

2261
01:35:30.866 --> 01:35:32.849
I don't think we have hard data on that.

2262
01:35:32.849 --> 01:35:37.849
The one thing that is quite evident is this prevalence,

2263
01:35:38.258 --> 01:35:42.008
massive prevalence of anxiety and depression.

2264
01:35:42.902 --> 01:35:45.482
And it's not the typical anxiety and depression,

2265
01:35:45.482 --> 01:35:49.217
because sometimes when you're in survivor mode,

2266
01:35:49.217 --> 01:35:51.128
you don't really have the time

2267
01:35:51.128 --> 01:35:54.535
to show the manifestation of depression.

2268
01:35:54.535 --> 01:35:57.486
So when you are always wondering,

2269
01:35:57.486 --> 01:36:00.433
what your children are going to eat the next day,

2270
01:36:00.433 --> 01:36:02.383
and when you're always wondering,

2271
01:36:02.383 --> 01:36:05.550
whether you're going to have a shelter tomorrow or not,

2272
01:36:05.550 --> 01:36:06.755
or whether your loved one

2273
01:36:06.755 --> 01:36:09.403
is going to be around your dinner table or not,

2274
01:36:09.403 --> 01:36:13.224
there's no time for you to sit back and feel bad.

2275
01:36:13.224 --> 01:36:15.807
There's this massive amount of anxiety

2276
01:36:15.807 --> 01:36:17.099
that people live with.

2277
01:36:17.099 --> 01:36:18.478
Yes, there are a lot of deaths,

2278
01:36:18.478 --> 01:36:20.642
because of cardiovascular disease,

2279
01:36:20.642 --> 01:36:23.021
and the other manifestations of stress and anxiety.

2280
01:36:23.021 --> 01:36:25.231
I don't think anybody has actually done work,

2281
01:36:25.231 --> 01:36:28.478
to look at the neurological manifestations of that.

2282
01:36:28.478 --> 01:36:32.297
And especially in the last 20 years with early deaths,

2283
01:36:32.297 --> 01:36:36.297
and people dying of easily preventable diseases.

2284
01:36:37.605 --> 01:36:39.383
They probably don't even get to that point,

2285
01:36:39.383 --> 01:36:41.380
where the neurodegeneration aspect

2286
01:36:41.380 --> 01:36:42.876
actually starts kicking in.

2287
01:36:42.876 --> 01:36:44.333
Just as a continuation of that.

2288
01:36:44.333 --> 01:36:45.502
I mean, that's a beautiful answer.

2289
01:36:45.502 --> 01:36:48.795
So I shouldn't, but I'll just give it a little bit.

2290
01:36:48.795 --> 01:36:50.411
So the human brain,

2291
01:36:50.411 --> 01:36:53.310
we're here outside of the intangible answers,

2292
01:36:53.310 --> 01:36:54.345
that why we're here,

2293
01:36:54.345 --> 01:36:57.472
the tangible is we're here because of the...

2294
01:36:57.472 --> 01:37:00.586
As much valued as we have for it's our brain, right?

2295
01:37:00.586 --> 01:37:01.952
Especially our feeling brain.

2296
01:37:01.952 --> 01:37:04.682
Dekar said (speaking in foreign language).

2297
01:37:04.682 --> 01:37:06.413
I say, (speaking in foreign language)

2298
01:37:06.413 --> 01:37:08.153
I feel therefore I am.

2299
01:37:08.153 --> 01:37:09.859
As much as we can feel, as much...

2300
01:37:09.859 --> 01:37:12.050
That's why the animal thing, that's why...

2301
01:37:12.050 --> 01:37:15.770
If you don't distill the cause to the base value,

2302
01:37:15.770 --> 01:37:19.897
which is ability to feel, it's meaningless.

2303
01:37:19.897 --> 01:37:24.564
So as far as feeling is concerned, yes that's the brain.

2304
01:37:25.716 --> 01:37:27.798
The brain is here to feel, but at the same time,

2305
01:37:27.798 --> 01:37:30.704
it's also here to explore.

2306
01:37:30.704 --> 01:37:35.574
Feel fully, and there are levels of it, and explore fully.

2307
01:37:35.574 --> 01:37:36.604
When the brain is not...

2308
01:37:36.604 --> 01:37:37.933
And this, we don't have data in Afghanistan,

2309
01:37:37.933 --> 01:37:39.596
but outside of Afghanistan,

2310
01:37:39.596 --> 01:37:43.096
when a brain is not exploring, it shrinks.

2311
01:37:44.269 --> 01:37:46.717
The moment the brain stops exploring,

2312
01:37:46.717 --> 01:37:49.496
and exploring could be anything thinking, reading,

2313
01:37:49.496 --> 01:37:50.613
playing music,

2314
01:37:50.613 --> 01:37:53.977
all of this stuff except for playing Sudoku, which I hate,

2315
01:37:53.977 --> 01:37:57.403
but all these manifestations of creativity,

2316
01:37:57.403 --> 01:38:00.065
of the mind being coming to the fore.

2317
01:38:00.065 --> 01:38:02.697
And if it's not doing that, it shrinks.

2318
01:38:02.697 --> 01:38:05.457
It has more consequence than eating bad.

2319
01:38:05.457 --> 01:38:06.375
And I'm a nutritionist.

2320
01:38:06.375 --> 01:38:09.272
I have a master's in nutrition, she has a master...

2321
01:38:09.272 --> 01:38:14.272
Inability to let the brain be creative, destroys the brain.

2322
01:38:14.860 --> 01:38:19.860
And we have entire 50% of the general population shrouding,

2323
01:38:20.060 --> 01:38:22.067
not being able to think.

2324
01:38:22.067 --> 01:38:23.792
You're killing them.

2325
01:38:23.792 --> 01:38:24.625
Yeah.

2326
01:38:24.625 --> 01:38:25.593
And that's true in America.

2327
01:38:25.593 --> 01:38:27.341
It's true everywhere.

2328
01:38:27.341 --> 01:38:32.107
So as far as why we're here is let people's creativity roam,

2329
01:38:32.107 --> 01:38:33.107
let it flourish.

2330
01:38:33.107 --> 01:38:34.611
Don't be scared.

2331
01:38:34.611 --> 01:38:36.028
We have latitude.

2332
01:38:38.637 --> 01:38:40.626
